--- against the other energy ---------------------------------------------
E_w1 of pten_mutants_soft_E2.csv vs dU of pten_single_mutants.csv, on the 380 mutants both scans contain.
Both are costs, so a POSITIVE correlation means they rank mutants the same way.
  pooled over all mutants: +0.631
  within site (centred ranks, 20 sites): +0.329
  per site, on the mean of log10: +0.848

--- per variant ----------------------------------------------------------
Each in-silico mutant matched to the same substitution in the two experiments. This is the
comparison the papers themselves make, and the one a per-site profile cannot: it asks whether
the energy ranks the 19 substitutions at a site, not just which sites are expensive.
                         experiment  variants matched  rho(-dU, score)  rho within site  sites  AUC(dU, damaging)  positives  labelled
abundance 2021 (VAMP-seq composite)               236           +0.141           +0.052     17             +0.614         76       209
          abundance 2018 (VAMP-seq)               211           +0.179           +0.043     16             +0.584         85       211
 activity (Mighell high-confidence)               320           +0.137           +0.067     18             +0.623        101       320

The last three columns are the energy used as a CLASSIFIER of the authors' own variant calls,
one call per experiment. AUC is the area under the ROC curve, equivalently the probability that
a randomly chosen damaging variant has a higher dU than a randomly chosen tolerated one. The label
is the DAMAGING outcome and the score is dU itself, so above 0.5 is the agreement direction and
0.5 is chance. Variants with no measurement are left out rather than counted as tolerated:
  abundance 2021 (VAMP-seq composite): damaging = low or possibly low (2021 classes), 76 of 209 labelled variants
  abundance 2018 (VAMP-seq): damaging = low or possibly low (2018 classes), 85 of 211 labelled variants
  activity (Mighell high-confidence): damaging = score < -1.11, 101 of 320 labelled variants

